 applied to multi-class prediction for the analysis of gene expression data</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2003</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>44</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12499291</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lewis</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A genetic algorithm for maximum-likelihood phylogeny inference using nucleotide sequence data</article-title><source>Mol. Biol. Evol.</source><year>1998</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>283</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9501494</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kosakovsky Pond</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Posada</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Gravenor</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Woelk</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Frost</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Automated phylogenetic detection of recombination using a genetic algorithm</article-title><source>Mol. Biol. Evol.</source><year>2006</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1891</fpage><lpage>1901</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16818476</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Syswerda</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A study of reproduction in generational and steady-state genetic algorithms</article-title><source>In Foundations of Genetic Algorithms</source><year>1991</year><comment>Morgan Kauffmann Publishers, San Mateo, USA, pp. 94&#x02013;101</comment></element-citation></ref><ref id="